 See [Graph state and channels](../models/README.md) for the full-state node
 contract, application-defined reducers, merge order, and write extraction limits.
+
+## Active-path joins
+
+`GraphBuilder(..., join_policy=JoinPolicy.ACTIVE)` opts into joins over active
+paths. Import `JoinPolicy` from `runengine.programs.graph.models.enums`. A node
+activated by one predecessor waits while another live frontier node can still
+reach it through forward dependencies. Unselected conditional paths do not block
+it. Unequal-length selected paths still join once after both finish. Deferred
+nodes are part of BSP's checkpoint position and survive restoration.
+
+The default `JoinPolicy.ALL` preserves static all-predecessor gating. Default
+serialization omits the new graph field and empty pending-node state, retaining
+legacy request/checkpoint shapes. New active-mode requests require matched
+coordinator code; update workers before enabling the option. Goto still directly
+activates its targets and FinishTraversal retains lifecycle ownership.
 
